{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical","lean:module:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.ratio_eq_iff_qb_three_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.ratio_eq_iff_qb_three_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.lean#L130-L149","doc":"**The gate.** The `N=2` and `N=3` Ocneanu weight ratios are equal **iff**\n`[3]_q = 0`.\n\nStated as an `iff` deliberately: it says exactly what would have to happen for\nthe two traces to be proportional, rather than asserting they are not. The\narchimedean file rules the right-hand side out. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_two_four_sub_one_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_two_four_sub_one_five","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.lean#L122-L128","doc":"**The identity.** `[2]_q [4]_q − [1]_q [5]_q = [3]_q`.\n\nThis is what replaces *\"differs at every `q` tested\"*: the discrepancy between\nthe two weight ratios is not merely nonzero on a sample, it is exactly `[3]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_shift_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_shift_identity","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.lean#L102-L120","doc":"**The general shift identity.** `[n+1]_q [n+3]_q − [n]_q [n+4]_q = [3]_q`\nfor **every** `n` — the right-hand side does not depend on `n`.\n\nThis is the statement the exclusion actually wants. Comparing the Ocneanu weight\nratio at `N` and at `N+1` reduces to this cross-product difference, and it is\n`[3]_q` at every `N`. So re-tuning does not fail to reproduce the `N = 2`\nweighting *only* at `N = 3`: **every** adjacent pair of `N` re-weights, and\nalways by the same amount. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_five_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_five_eq","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.lean#L97-L100","doc":"`[5]_q = q⁴ + q² + 1 + q⁻² + q⁻⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_four_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_four_eq","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.lean#L92-L95","doc":"`[4]_q = q³ + q + q⁻¹ + q⁻³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_three_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_three_eq","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.lean#L86-L90","doc":"`[3]_q = q² + 1 + q⁻²`. This is the quantity the whole comparison reduces\nto, so it is worth having in expanded form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_two_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_two_eq","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.lean#L81-L84","doc":"`[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` — the convention-fixing case (AGENTS.md §7aa). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.sub_inv_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.sub_inv_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.lean#L74-L79","doc":"The `q`-bracket denominator is nonzero exactly when `q² ≠ 1` — which is, by\n`QOU.Eightfold.HeckeBraidingNonSymmetric.double_braiding_eq_one_iff`, exactly\nthe condition that the braiding is **not** symmetric. The `q`-integers are\nwell-defined precisely on the non-symmetric locus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.lean#L69-L72","doc":"**The consolidation.** `qb` is the canonical balanced `q`-integer. The two\nbodies differ only by `q⁻¹ ^ n` versus `(q ^ n)⁻¹`, which `inv_pow` identifies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.qb","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional.lean#L56-L67","doc":"The balanced `q`-integer `[n]_q = (qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ)/(q − q⁻¹)`, the convention in\nwhich `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` (AGENTS.md §7aa).\n\n> **This duplicates the canonical `QOU.QInteger.qIntBal`** and is kept only so\n> the proofs below can `simp [qb]` down to the literal body, exactly as\n> `QOU.BraidKnot.AJTrefoil.qInt` is kept for the same reason. The consolidation\n> is the equation `qb_eq_canonical` immediately below: same function, one\n> canonical meaning, no proof touched. Flagged on PR #5746 by the agent working\n> bean `qou-qint`, which is actively bridging duplicate `q`-integer definitions\n> — this file was written without checking for one, and would otherwise have\n> been another. ","signatureChunk":0}]}